  "briefing": "## Situation\nDusk, clear. Post Alpha is on open farmland. Hostile drones have been using a loud, high decoy to draw attention while a second drone comes in low from another direction. Birds, civilian hobby drones and our own patrol drone are also up.\n## Mission\nDetect, identify and defeat every hostile before it reaches Post Alpha. Leave birds, civilians and friendlies alone. Contact reports are expected: send one for every threat track (R).\n## ROE\nWEAPONS TIGHT — intercept only tracks you have classified as a threat type and declared HOSTILE. No intercepts inside the marked no-kinetic zones (settlements).\n## Assets\n- Radar, EO/IR camera and RF detector on high ground near the asset\n- RF jammer, 2.0 km, ±10° sector, 10 s cycle\n- GNSS spoofer, 2.0 km, ±10° sector, 15 s cycle\n- Interceptor, 1.5 km, 3 rounds, 6 s reload\n## Intel\nExpect an RF-loud drone high to the north-east first. Do not let it hold your attention: the real threat may be low, fast and silent to the RF detector, and on the opposite side.",
